<Layout title="What Is the Robux Tax? A Plain-English Guide" description="What people mean by the Robux tax, how it changes what you keep, and how to price items around it." path="/guides/what-is-robux-tax" schema={schema}>
<h1>What Is the Robux Tax?</h1>
<p>The "Robux tax" is the community's name for the share Roblox keeps when a creator sells something. It is not a government tax. It is a platform fee, and it changes how much of each sale you actually receive.</p>
<h2>Why it matters for pricing</h2>
<p>If you want to keep a specific amount, you have to charge more than that amount. Work backwards from your target with the <a href="/">Robux Tax Calculator</a> instead of guessing.</p>
<h2>From Robux to real money</h2>
<p>Robux you keep can later be turned into cash through DevEx, which has its own rate. Try the <a href="/robux-to-usd-calculator">Robux to USD calculator</a>, or see your estimate in <a href="/robux-to-eur-calculator">euros</a> or <a href="/robux-to-gbp-calculator">pounds</a>.</p>
<p class="small">Fees and rates change. Always confirm on Roblox's <a href="https://create.roblox.com/docs" rel="noopener" target="_blank">official creator docs</a>.</p>
<Faq items={faq} />
</Layout>
